From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:29:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] UNFILED 89 review: a test that catches the defect;
 deterministic, not exact

- The per-rank sum is a helper, _sum_abs_deterministic, tested on the same data
  at 8 memory offsets (n = 384, 1536, 20011). A NORM_1 version of it fails that
  test every time on AVX-512 OpenBLAS (2 or 3 distinct values per size). The
  old test compared against a recomputation through getSubVector, which always
  copies, and development passed it 5 of 12 runs serially.
- The operator test now calls the scale on freshly assembled operators (10
  ptaps, 3 calls each).
- "Exact" is now "deterministic": fsum of per-rank fsums, divided by n, rounds
  more than once, so the scale is reproducible but not the correctly rounded
  mean.
- The gather is on the operator's communicator, not COMM_WORLD.
- The CHANGES title says the rotated operator is bit-identical, since VecMDot's
  gemv path is alignment-dependent too.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
